-- §8 I4 -- A BARE METHOD OCCURRENCE NAMES ITS OWN CLASS, NOT A SAME-SPELLED FOREIGN
-- ONE. This is the SURVIVING half of #1438 after U1b (#1482) drained the
-- signature-`=>` half (`i4-xmod-sig-constraint-foreign-iface-rejected`), and it is
-- the positive guard `test/must_fail_fixtures/1507-xmod-iface-name-collision-
-- method-occurrence` owed when U1c (#1507) drained it -- a pin asserts a bug still
-- reproduces, so a fix removes it and the S0 has NO guard unless a positive row
-- replaces it.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, HAND-DERIVED FROM DICT-SEMANTICS §8 I4, not read off a binary:
--   1. `zmod` declares its own `interface Sizer a where bulk`, imports nothing, so
--      the `bulk x` occurrence inside `useBulk`'s own body unambiguously denotes
--      `zmod.Sizer` (§8 I4 qualification 1: a same-module declaration wins, and
--      there is nothing else in scope to compete with it anyway).
--   2. `main` calls `useBulk 3`, instantiating the method occurrence's dispatch
--      type at `Int`, posing the goal `zmod.Sizer Int`.
--   3. `match(IE, zmod.Sizer Int)` is EMPTY. The graph's only `impl Sizer Int`
--      belongs to `amod.Sizer` -- a different declaration whose method set
--      (`weight`) is disjoint from `zmod.Sizer`'s (`bulk`). An impl of one class is
--      not an impl of another that merely shares a spelling.
--   => REJECT, `No impl of Sizer for Int` (T-NO-IMPL). There is no value to pin --
--      the program never runs.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS ROW GUARDS, MEASURED ON A main-BUILT BINARY BEFORE U1c: `check`
-- exit 0 printing `main : Unit` (SILENT ACCEPT); `run` E-PANIC `unbound
-- identifier: bulk` (dict-passing handed `useBulk` a dictionary shaped for
-- `amod.Sizer`, i.e. `{weight}`, and projecting `bulk` out of it found nothing);
-- `build` exit 0 with a binary that SEGFAULTS at 139. That was #1438's surviving
-- reach. If a later change re-widens the METHOD-OCCURRENCE channel
-- (`recordImplObligation`) back to a bare spelling, THIS ROW GOES
-- GREEN-BY-ACCEPTING and the S0 is back -- which is exactly what it exists to
-- stop.
--
-- ⚠️ TOPOLOGICALLY DISCRIMINATING BY CONSTRUCTION, same reasoning as the
-- signature-constraint sibling: the goal is posed and elaborated when `zmod` is
-- processed; `amod`'s foreign impl lives in a module `zmod` does not import. A
-- shape whose goal is posed only in `main` would be a false null, because `main`
-- is always topologically LAST and therefore always sees the whole universe.
--
-- ⚠️ Distinct from `i4-xmod-sig-constraint-foreign-iface-rejected` (the sibling
-- row): that one reaches the collision through a constrained BINDING's `=>` slot
-- (`funConstraintIfacesRef` + `schemeObligationsRef`, U1b's channel). This one
-- reaches it through the bare METHOD OCCURRENCE itself
-- (`recordImplObligation`'s `pushPendingObl`, U1c's channel) -- `useBulk` here
-- carries no signature at all, so there is no `=>` slot for U1b's fix to touch.
import amod
import zmod.{useBulk}

main = println (useBulk 3)
